{
  "sample_rate": 48000,
  "bpm": 120,
  "duration_s": 240,
  "input_wav": "host/render/scenarios/assets/in_drone.wav",
  "init": [
    {
      "_comment": "Task 12 fix round (spec 2026-08-12-modulation-pace S3.3): review found the original single-phase render left engine_a/engine_b to the terrain's own RNG draw (roles_of(), engine/flow/terrain.cpp:262-269) -- for terrain F1-0000FACE-000000000000 that draw happens to be SYNTH on BOTH decks (checked directly against roles_of() with a scratch probe), so the file proved nothing about a BBD or Sampler deck. Fixed by pinning engines explicitly rather than trusting the draw to stay put -- a future terrain change could otherwise silently break this file's whole purpose. Explicit set_engine calls placed AFTER flow_wake survive the flow layer's own per-tick engine push: Flow::wake()'s recompute_and_push(true) force-pushes P_ENGINE_A/B once (flow.cpp:96-123), but every later tick only re-pushes a param when its recomputed value differs from Flow's OWN last-pushed record (flow.cpp:639-643) -- and with no flow_new/flow_new_partial/flow_undo event anywhere in this file, that recomputed value never moves, so Flow never notices (or fights) a scenario override that only touches the live Instrument. Same mechanism already verified for set_pace itself in the task-12 review.",
      "action": "flow_wake",
      "value": "F1-0000FACE-000000000000"
    },
    {
      "action": "flow_macro",
      "slot": 0,
      "value": 0.5
    },
    {
      "action": "flow_macro",
      "slot": 1,
      "value": 0.5
    },
    {
      "action": "flow_macro",
      "slot": 2,
      "value": 0.5
    },
    {
      "action": "flow_macro",
      "slot": 3,
      "value": 0.5
    },
    {
      "action": "flow_macro",
      "slot": 4,
      "value": 0.5
    },
    {
      "action": "flow_macro",
      "slot": 5,
      "value": 0.5
    },
    {
      "action": "set_pace",
      "value": 0.5
    },
    {
      "_comment": "Phase 1 (0-120s): deck A pinned BBD, deck B pinned SAMPLER. Both read the SAME input_wav each sample (Instrument::process passes one in_l/in_r pair to both parts, engine/instrument.cpp:200-213). in_drone.wav is only 48s long and the host does not loop input_wav (main.cpp zero-pads past end-of-file), which would leave the back half of this 120s phase unfed -- so deck A additionally pulls deck B's own output (set_excitation_sources, other_deck=true; Instrument wires Part::set_deck_in every sample regardless, instrument.cpp:194, and Part::process only USES it when _src_deck is set, part.h:367-370). Deck B's sampler loops its recorded buffer on its own once something is captured (see the record burst below), so from t=8s on, deck A's BBD is fed a continuously-circulating loop instead of running dry. Every other voice/target parameter (voice attack/decay/resonance/sub/filt, and the five LANE_SOURCE..LEVEL target bases) is left to the flow layer's own terrain-driven pushes -- P_ATTACK_A/P_DECAY_A/etc are ordinary flow params (engine/flow/flow_params.h:84-88, 175-184) that the terrain already pushes for whichever engine is live, exactly as a real Glow patch would drive a BBD or Sampler deck it randomly landed on.",
      "action": "set_engine",
      "part": 0,
      "value": "bbd"
    },
    {
      "action": "set_engine",
      "part": 1,
      "value": "sampler"
    },
    {
      "action": "set_excitation_sources",
      "part": 0,
      "flag": false,
      "ivalue": 1
    },
    {
      "_comment": "Feedback raised from the 0.95 boot default toward sampler_bloom.json's near-unity 0.971 rung, so the captured loop keeps circulating audibly across the whole 120s phase (and on into deck A's BBD feed) instead of decaying out partway through the sweep.",
      "action": "sampler_feedback",
      "part": 1,
      "value": 0.97
    }
  ],
  "events": [
    {
      "_comment": "Deck B (SAMPLER) records ~7s of the drone near the top of phase 1, then plays the captured loop back for the rest of the phase -- same capture shape as sampler_bloom.json.",
      "t": 1.0,
      "action": "sampler_record",
      "part": 1,
      "flag": true
    },
    {
      "t": 8.0,
      "action": "sampler_record",
      "part": 1,
      "flag": false
    },
    {
      "_comment": "Phase 2 (120-240s): deck A switches to SYNTH (Part::set_engine crossfades over ~385 samples, ~8ms -- inaudible against a 120s sweep) so the render also covers spec S3.3's third consumer, the synth voice envelopes that rescale with the cycle (synth_engine.cpp:275-276). Deck A's own flow-driven PITCH lane keeps firing chords in FLOW mode regardless of which engine is live (Part::_fire_trigger is Part-level, not engine-specific) -- this is the exact mechanism that made the original single-phase render (both decks SYNTH by the terrain's draw) audible with no manual trigger_* event anywhere in this file. Deck B is silenced for this phase (LEVEL target parked at 0 and its lane deactivated) so deck A's synth voices are heard in isolation, the same isolation bbd_pitch_bend.json and sampler_bloom.json use for their own single-deck listening checks.",
      "t": 120.0,
      "action": "set_engine",
      "part": 0,
      "value": "synth"
